s fixed: |3000 - 1000| + |-3000 - 1000| = 2000 + 4000 = 6000. Therefore, the sum is the same regardless of which lottery is considered. So the reason would be indifferent between A and B because the sum of pairwise differences is equal. But the reason says it prefers the one with the more favorable sum — implying that if one has a larger sum, it is preferred. However, in this case, the sum is the same. So the decision reason does not favor either — it would be indifferent. Thus, the decision reason is applicable and can be evaluated, but it results in indifference between A and B due to equal sum of pairwise differences.",
